// THE GENERIC RUNG OF THE INLINE-LITERAL-UNION ELEMENT FAMILY — CLOSED.
//
// This file was `@no-instantiate`: `vl check` rc 0, `vl build` reporting success, and the
// engine refusing the module with `type mismatch: expected (ref $type), found i32`. It now
// runs and prints `b`, and the pin is the behaviour rather than the refusal.
//
// THE DISAGREEMENT, unchanged and still the family's root: `ctxKeepsLitUnion` PRESERVES a
// literal union's members at `RC_ELEM` and SOFTENS them at `RC_ROOT`, so `("a" | "b")[]` is
// an array of interned i32 ATOMS while `"a" | "b"` in a result position is a string ref.
// The two meet at every read of an element, and the fix is the boundary WIDEN that turns
// the atom into the string the slot wants.
//
// WHAT ACTUALLY WITHHELD THE WIDEN, and it is one fact with three consumers. A
// MONOMORPHIZED instance's body is a FRESH CLONE minted after the checker ran, so a
// parameter reference inside it carries NO RECORDED TYPE — and all three of the widen's
// questions were asked of the recorded type:
//
//   1. `exprIsLitAtom`'s Index arm — WHETHER to widen. Answered false, so no widen: the
//      raw i32 flowed into the string slot. That was the silent invalid module.
//   2. `emitAtomToStr` — WHICH members to widen with. Fixing (1) alone moved the failure to
//      a loud `literal-union string widening with no members`, which is better and still
//      wrong.
//   3. `retWidensAtomToStr` — whether to RESERVE the string-op scratch frame the widen
//      writes through. Fixing (1) and (2) moved it again, to `unknown local 4`.
//
// Each now falls back to the receiver's PARAM ANNOTATION, which mono DOES synthesize
// (`nret`/`nps` are minted with the substituted type). That is the architecture's own
// carrier: there is no re-check pass over instances, so an annotation is what a
// monomorphized body has instead of recorded types.
//
// THE NAMED-ALIAS CONTROL was green throughout and shows why this rung survived the other
// two: `K` in result position reps as the ATOM, so both ends already agree and no widen is
// wanted at all. Only the INLINE spelling needs one.
//
// THE REST OF THE FAMILY: `std:array`'s `indexOf` / `lastIndexOf` / `includes` / `count` /
// `reduce` / `reverse` over an inline-litunion array all ran as a consequence of this. The
// two boundaries this header used to leave open — binding an element read to a local, and
// element ASSIGNMENT — are CLOSED as well, by the same annotation fallback generalized to
// every storage class a name can resolve to; `generic-litunion-element-bind-and-store.vl`
// beside this file carries them, and `sorted` runs.
// @run
// @log b

function pick<T>(self: T[]): T { self[0] }

const tags: ("a" | "b")[] = ["b", "a", "b"]
print(pick(tags))
